phi-adapter-fritz (0.0~git202609081156.67d8a88-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * No Qt. The loop and the timers come from phi-runtime through the SDK, HTTP
    with digest authentication from the SDK's client, JSON from nlohmann. The
    nested event loop every request used to run inside is gone with it.
  * Three of the six actions this adapter issued do not exist on the router in
    the field, and it had no way of noticing. GetHostListPath is
    X_AVM-DE_GetHostListPath here; its failure fell through to one SOAP call
    per host - 110 of them, twelve times a minute, measured at 31 MB an hour.
    The poll now asks GetSpecificHostEntry per tracked address instead, and the
    full table only when browseHosts is pressed.
  * GetAddonInfos and X_AVM-DE_GetAutoUpdateInfo are Invalid Action here, which
    is why tx_rate and rx_rate had never carried a value. The rate is derived
    from the byte counters, which this router does implement. An action that
    says Invalid Action is not issued again, and a channel that cannot be
    filled is not advertised.
  * The poll is split by rate of change: uptime, tracked hosts and the counters
    every interval; WLAN, firmware and update state once a minute.
  * Values and device descriptors are only sent when they changed.
  * "Test connection" works at factory scope, where it is declared. The factory
    hook was never overridden, so the SDK answered "Factory action handler not
    implemented" to it.
  * SOAP parameters are XML-escaped.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 11:56:37 +0200

